-- RECONCILED Scenario 153: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT `the House is taken to have adjourned` `the Senate` `the House expires` EQUALS JUST FALSE`; triaged against the text: test-author wording: the encoding's stated convention for 'the section does not give it' is NOTHING from a MAYBE function; s 2M(3)(c) (L233) is silent on a Senate that expires, so NOTHING is the accurate answer. The reviewer agrees (its triage 2.1)
#ASSERT `the House is taken to have adjourned` `the Senate` `the House expires` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ===== PART 3: commencement =====
-- Scenario 154 (s 3): expressed to come into operation on 2026-07-01 -> start of that day
#ASSERT `the moment the enactment comes into operation` `Act` (`commencement on a particular day` (Date 1 7 2026)) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (`Moment in a day` OF (Date 1 7 2026), 0, 0, 0)
-- Scenario 155 (s 3): "commence" wording gives the same moment
#ASSERT `the moment the enactment comes into operation` `Act` (`commencement on a particular day` (Date 1 7 2026)) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (`Moment in a day` OF (Date 1 7 2026), 0, 0, 0)
-- Scenario 156 (s 3): a provision (not the Act) commencing on the day: same moment
