-- RECONCILED Scenario 547: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT `the thing is done within the time allowed` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 4 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) `no closures` EQUALS FALSE`; triaged against the text: arguable fork, not a test-author error and not an encoder error: the reviewer reads s 36(2) (L814-818) literally (only the original last day and the next non-rest day are permitted, so the Sunday between is not); the encoding extends the period to the rolled day, so every day up to it is in time (the Example at L819 does not discuss the days between). Registered as fork F9 in NOTES.md with both readings; the reviewer's expectation was FALSE
#ASSERT `the thing is done within the time allowed` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 4 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) `no closures` EQUALS TRUE
